From: =?UTF-8?q?=C3=98yvind=20Harboe?= <oyvind.harboe@zylin.com>
Subject: [PATCH] ram: the option tests route their blocks through
 generate_ram
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Every option test now builds its block with generate_ram, so it is
placed, given its power grid, pins and fillers, and routed, and then
checks what the option computes on the routed block.
src/ram/test/routed.tcl holds generate_ram's arguments for asap7 and
Nangate45, and routed::check: every signal net with two or more pins
has a wire, and detailed routing ran and left no violations.

What changed besides the command:

- banks and bank_column_layout use 32 words: at 8 words in four banks,
  two side by side, the block was a strip 36 um wide and 1.35 um tall
  whose east edge had six pin slots for nine address pins.
- service_columns counts fillers and taps as empty sites: in a routed
  block they fill the columns the option leaves.
- periphery_unplaced stays on generate_ram_netlist: generate_ram does
  not take -periphery unplaced.
- option_errors runs generate_ram, and adds -zero_word past the last
  word (RAM-0059), -register_read_address 2 (RAM-0071), an unreadable
  -tracks file (RAM-0097) and -periphery unplaced (RAM-0098).

Tested: src/ram/test, all 21 tests.

Commit 22 of 23 in OpenROAD #11723, carried here from it. Not
upstreamed; retires at a //:bump onto an OpenROAD that has it.
